<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! sense.holder.quiesces ~ the sovereign parallel of the guest quiesce

`lares sense quiesce` pauses the hook legs (the memory sensorium alone owns them) and drains every holder sitting under the sensorium's root, confirming zero; `hold=true` keeps the hooks paused. A leading sensorium name (`lares sense <sensorium> <verb>`) addresses any named sensorium; bare, the verb reads `memory`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ quiesce · hold

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`quiesce` params=`~ drain the memory sensorium`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`hold` params=`hold/true ~ drain and keep the hooks paused`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ hold · sensorium-root

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`hold` params=`~ keep the hooks paused after the drain`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`sensorium-root` params=`takes/host-path ~ the sensorium's root; the leading sensorium name threads it, absent the memory sensorium`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ local

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`local` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ signals this host's sensorium processes; this handler checks no ocap`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

